.TH "Docv::CrystalPages::Roff" "3cr" "2026-11-03" "docv 0.1.0" "docv API Reference"
.SH "NAME"
Docv::CrystalPages::Roff \- roff escaping for man(7) output.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBrequire "docv/cli"\fR
.sp
\fBmodule Docv::CrystalPages::Roff\fR
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
roff escaping for man(7) output.
.SH "CONSTANTS"
.TP 4
\fBGLYPHS\fR
.RS
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
GLYPHS = {
  \(aq\e\e\(aq => "\e\ee",
  \(aq\-\(aq => "\e\e\-",
  \(aq\e\(aq\(aq => "\e\e(aq",
  \(aq\(ga\(aq => "\e\e(ga",
  \(aq\(ti\(aq => "\e\e(ti",
  \(aq\(ha\(aq => "\e\e(ha",
}
.EE
.RE
.PP
Characters roff reads as escapes or typesets as typographic glyphs,
with their literal spellings.
.RE
.TP 4
\fBINDENT = 4\fR
Indentation of nested blocks, in ens.
.SH "CLASS METHODS"
.PP
\fBdef self.bold(text : String) : String\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef self.escape(char : Char, io : IO) : Nil\fR
Writes \fIchar\fR so roff prints it literally; non\-ASCII characters become
\fB\%\e[uXXXX]\fR, valid in any encoding.
.PP
\fBdef self.escape(text : String, io : IO) : Nil\fR
.PP
\fBdef self.escape(text : String) : String\fR
.TP 4
\fBdef self.line(text : String, io : IO) : Nil\fR
Writes \fItext\fR as one text line that is never read as a request.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.lines(text : String, io : IO) : Nil\fR
Writes \fItext\fR as literal lines for a no\-fill display.
.TP 4
\fBdef self.quote(text : String) : String\fR
Double\-quoted macro argument.
